<!-- QUICKTEST_POSTSETUP_CRASH_1 -> src fix. authored 2026-09-12 (FOUNDRY).

     THE BUG, MEASURED not guessed:
     the live 592-mod def dump (DefDump/captures/2026-09-12T11-53-17Z,
     fingerprint-matched to the exact mod set that reproduced the crash twice)
     shows ResearchProjectDef RR_ElectricityBasics ("Research Reinvented:
     Stepping Stones", petetimessix.researchreinvented.steppingstones) with
     prerequisites containing ITSELF:

         "prerequisites": ["RR_ElectricityBasics"]

     A DFS cycle check over every ResearchProjectDef's prerequisites in that
     dump found exactly one cycle in the whole 397-project graph, and this is
     it (self loop, length 1).

     On disk (workshop 2868389782, v1.6/Defs/ResearchProjectDefs_Electricity.xml)
     RR_ElectricityBasics's OWN prerequisites list reads plain li Smithing li,
     not itself: the self-reference is injected by a PATCH, not authored
     directly. That same mod's Patches_ResearchProjectDefs.xml uses a custom
     operation class (RR.PatchOperationResearchPrereg) to re-point every
     project that used to require vanilla "Electricity" onto
     RR_ElectricityBasics instead (its "stepping stones" mechanism); the exact
     step by which that walk also lands on RR_ElectricityBasics itself lives
     inside that closed custom PatchOperation class and was not traced
     further. The OBSERVED RESULT is what this fix acts on, confirmed against
     the live dump above, independent of which upstream step causes it.

     WHY THIS CRASHES THE ENGINE, VERIFIED against 1.6 decompiled source
     (RimSage, RimWorld/ResearchManager.cs:403-410):

         public void FinishProject(ResearchProjectDef proj, ...)
         {
             if (proj.prerequisites != null)
                 for (int i = 0; i < proj.prerequisites.Count; i++)
                     if (!proj.prerequisites[i].IsFinished)
                         FinishProject(proj.prerequisites[i], ...);   // recurse
             ...
             progress[proj] = proj.baseCost;   // proj marked finished ONLY here, after the loop
         }

     No cycle or visited-set guard anywhere in this method. For a
     self-referencing prerequisite, proj.prerequisites[0] IS proj, and proj is
     not yet IsFinished (that only happens after the loop returns), so the
     very first prerequisite check recurses into FinishProject(proj) again,
     with the identical unfinished state, forever. This is unbounded
     recursion with no termination condition: a StackOverflowException, which
     .NET cannot catch or log (not even a top-level try/catch), terminating
     the whole process immediately and silently.

     This matches every symptom QUICKTEST_POSTSETUP_CRASH_1 recorded: no
     managed exception in Player.log, no crash-handler line, RimWorldWin64
     confirmed gone within seconds, right after a burst of real research
     completions (the leaf and earlier prerequisites in whatever chain
     eventually reaches this node finish and log normally on the way down and
     back up the recursion; the self-loop node itself never returns, so it
     logs nothing further before the crash, exactly "six research completed
     lines in a row, then the log ends abruptly").

     RR_ElectricityBasics is tagged ClassicStart, i.e. a project vanilla or
     scenario auto-setup pre-completes for a non-tribal quickstart, squarely
     in the path rimworld/start_debug_game_ready's own auto-research walks,
     and squarely NOT in the path of loading the real CANONICAL_ASHKARR save
     (whose research was already resolved turn by turn, never re-walking
     FinishProject's prerequisite recursion on a fresh cold graph). That is
     exactly the asymmetry the item recorded: quicktest crashes, the real
     save does not.

     THE FIX
     =======
     Remove ONLY the self-referencing li from RR_ElectricityBasics's own
     prerequisites list. Every other prerequisite (Smithing, on disk) and
     every consumer that requires RR_ElectricityBasics is untouched; this
     costs no content, it removes a cycle that could never have been a real
     research requirement in the first place (a project cannot legitimately
     require itself).

     MayRequire petetimessix.researchreinvented.steppingstones: a no-op, not
     an error, if that mod is inactive. Load order: this mod
     (mandrake.rm.patches) loads last, after every research-reinvented patch
     that could plausibly (re)create this node, so this is the final word on
     the def.

     VERIFY AFTER THE NEXT LOAD
     ===========================
     Re-run the DFS cycle check in this commit's investigation against a
     fresh def dump: 0 cycles over ResearchProjectDef.prerequisites. Then
     rimworld/start_debug_game_ready should reach programState Playing
     without RimWorldWin64 disappearing; verify 3x in a row per the item's
     own criteria before closing QUICKTEST_POSTSETUP_CRASH_1.
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional" MayRequire="petetimessix.researchreinvented.steppingstones">
    <xpath>Defs/ResearchProjectDef[defName="RR_ElectricityBasics"]/prerequisites/li[text()="RR_ElectricityBasics"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationRemove">
      <xpath>Defs/ResearchProjectDef[defName="RR_ElectricityBasics"]/prerequisites/li[text()="RR_ElectricityBasics"]</xpath>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
